d put pressure on the  kiev government so i think these phases  are going to unfold they are they are  deliberate and sanctions are going to  have absolutely no impact  on the plan that putin is executing  would anything have an impact i mean you  know president biden had this moment to  speak moments ago i just want to play a  little bit of what he said and then i  want to ask you you know  what can be done really at this point  watch  who in the lord's name does putin think  gives him the right to declare  new so-called countries  on territory that belong to his  neighbors  this is a flagrant violation of  international law and demands a firm  response from the international  community so general we know that  president that putin doesn't see it that  way he detailed in great uh exhaustive  essay  all the reasons that he thinks ukraine  is part of russia he believes it always  has been and he blamed you know former  soviet leaders for giving it away it was  very i mean interesting from a historic  perspective but so you hear president  biden they're saying you know that it  won't stand essentially but but how do  you  what changes that  well putin really  has a vision here and he's revealed it a  couple of times once in the in the  missive that he wrote last july  in 2021 uh which he contributed to  significantly 5 000 words and so many  hour-long speech in the nfc meeting  yesterday and when i look at that when i  boil it down to simplicity  uh what what he's about he he's taking  the post-cold war boundaries and  reconstructing them  because he absolutely believes when the  coal when the soviet union collapsed the  united states led an expansion into  eastern europe with nato at the expense  of russia and their security and he  wants a new security arrangements and he  wants to address those boundaries and  that's his vision and he starts with  ukraine and belarus and acquiring both  of those under his orbit is formidable  and anybody that thinks he's not going 